#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:12
msgid "Replaces the small line at the bottom left of every admin screen (\"Thank you for creating with WordPress\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:13
msgid "Everyone who works in the admin sees your text instead, for example a link to your support. Basic formatting and links are allowed. Leave it empty to keep the WordPress line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:16
msgid "Removes the WordPress version number from the bottom right of every admin screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:17
msgid "Editors no longer see which version runs and the footer looks cleaner. The version stays visible on the Updates screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:20
msgid "Hides the \"Screen Options\" tab at the top right of the admin screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:21
msgid "Nobody can change which columns and boxes a screen shows or how many items a list has per page. Choices already saved stay in force."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:22
msgid "You hide it from yourself too. Turn this off when you need to change a list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:25
msgid "Hides the \"Help\" tab at the top right of the admin screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:26
msgid "The built-in WordPress help panels are not offered any more. The screens work as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:27
msgid "Leave it off when your editors use the built-in help."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:30
msgid "Turns on the settings of the login page below: layout, logo, texts and colors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:31
msgid "The login, lost password and registration screens get your look. Turned off, WordPress shows its own login page and the settings below are kept but not used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:32
msgid "Light text on a light background (or the reverse) makes the form hard to read. Check the page in a private window after each change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:35
msgid "The image shown above the login form instead of the WordPress logo."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:36
msgid "People see your brand on the login page. In the split layout the logo can also appear over the media panel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:37
msgid "Leave it empty to show the WordPress logo, or hide the logo with the login form options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:40
msgid "Extra switches for the login form. \"Hide login logo\" removes the logo above the form completely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:41
msgid "The form starts straight with the fields, which suits a page where the logo is already part of the background."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:44
msgid "Ticks the \"Remember me\" box on the login form in advance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:45
msgid "People stay signed in for two weeks instead of until they close the browser, unless they untick the box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:46
msgid "On a shared computer someone may forget to untick it and leave their account open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:49
msgid "How round the corners of the login box are, in pixels."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:50
msgid "0 gives sharp corners, 8 to 16 a soft look, a large number a very round box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:53
msgid "How the background image of the classic login layout fills the screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:54
msgid "\"Cover\" fills the whole screen and may crop the edges. \"Fit inside\" shows the whole picture and leaves bands of the background color. \"Repeat\" tiles a small picture as a pattern."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:57
msgid "Chooses what the panel next to the login form shows in the split layout: an MP4 video, a picture or a YouTube video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:58
msgid "The field for the chosen type appears below. A video plays without sound in a loop."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:59
msgid "A large video slows down the login page, especially on a phone. Keep it short and small, or use a picture."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:62
msgid "The YouTube video that plays in the media panel. Paste the address of the video or only its ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:63
msgid "The video plays muted in a loop next to the form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:64
msgid "The login page loads content from YouTube, so YouTube can see the visitors of the login page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:67
msgid "Draws the login logo over the media panel in the split layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:68
msgid "The logo is shown once, over the picture or video. Turned off, it sits as a small round badge above the form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:71
msgid "Turns on the tidy-up of the bar at the top of the screen. The options under it only work while this is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:72
msgid "The bar gets shorter: updates move to the right, the site name becomes an icon and plugin items fold under a plus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:73
msgid "Turn it off to get the WordPress bar back as it was. The settings below are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:76
msgid "Your own image in place of the WordPress logo at the left end of the bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:77
msgid "The bar shows your brand. A small square image works best, a large one is scaled down."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:80
msgid "Hides the chosen items of the bar, for example the WordPress logo, the comments or the \"New\" menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:81
msgid "Fewer items for everybody who sees the bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:82
msgid "Hiding the Updates item means people no longer see the badge about pending updates in the bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:85
msgid "Moves the items with the number of updates and comments from the left part of the bar to the right."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:86
msgid "The left side keeps only what you use to navigate, the notifications sit next to your account on the right."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:89
msgid "Folds the items that plugins add to the bar into one \"+\" menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:90
msgid "The bar stays short even with many plugins. Items you list as \"keep on the bar\" stay visible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:91
msgid "A plugin item you need often is one click further, and counters that plugins show in the bar are hidden. Add such an item to the keep list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:94
msgid "Shows the site name in the bar as a small link icon on the right instead of a long text on the left."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:95
msgid "More room on the left. The link still opens the front page of the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:98
msgid "Hides the icons in front of the items of the left menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:99
msgid "The menu shows only text. The icon color setting is not used while the icons are hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:102
msgid "The width of the left menu in pixels. WordPress uses 160, you can set 120 to 300."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:103
msgid "A wider menu fits long item names on one line, a narrower one leaves more room for the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:104
msgid "With a very narrow menu long names are cut or wrapped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:107
msgid "Draws a modern set of line icons in place of the old WordPress menu icons."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:108
msgid "The menu looks more uniform. Icons without a replacement stay as they were, so nothing goes missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:111
msgid "Takes the notices of WordPress and plugins away from the top of the admin screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:112
msgid "The screens stay clean. By default the notices move to a tray instead of disappearing, and the history tab keeps what was shown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:113
msgid "Important warnings (a failed backup, an expired licence) may be overlooked. Look into the tray and the history from time to time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:116
msgid "Adds a search field to the top of the admin that finds posts, pages and other content from any screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:117
msgid "Editors jump to an item without opening its list first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:120
msgid "Chooses which kinds of content the quick search looks through."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:121
msgid "Fewer types give shorter, more relevant results. A type that is not ticked is never offered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:124
msgid "Shows the current time of the server in the admin bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:125
msgid "Handy when you schedule posts or read logs, because the server time can differ from your own time zone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:128
msgid "Where the server clock is shown: as a small pill in the bar or inside the \"+\" menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/AdminCustomiser/help.php:129
msgid "The pill is always visible, the plus menu keeps the bar shorter."
msgstr ""

