#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:12
msgid "WordPress stops installing new versions of itself by itself. You can still update by hand in Dashboard > Updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:13
msgid "The site stays on the version it has now until somebody updates it. Visitors notice nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:14
msgid "WordPress releases fix security holes several times a year. A site that is never updated by hand slowly becomes an easy target for hackers. Turn on the security exception below unless somebody else takes care of updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:15
msgid "Leave it off when nobody checks the site regularly, so the security releases arrive on their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:18
msgid "Chooses which WordPress releases are blocked: all of them, only major releases (new features, for example 6.8 to 6.9) or only minor releases (small fixes, for example 6.8.1 to 6.8.2)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:19
msgid "Blocking only major releases is the usual compromise: the site keeps getting small fixes but never changes behavior overnight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:20
msgid "Minor releases carry the security fixes. Blocking them (or all releases) leaves known holes open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:23
msgid "Even with core updates disabled, WordPress still installs the small security releases by itself. Major releases stay blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:24
msgid "You keep full control over big changes and still get the urgent security fixes without lifting a finger."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:25
msgid "Only when you test and install every release yourself, including the small ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:28
msgid "Plugins are no longer updated automatically. You can still update them by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:29
msgid "A plugin never changes without you knowing, so an update cannot break the site while you are away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:30
msgid "Outdated plugins are the most common way a site gets hacked. Nobody installs the fixes unless you do it by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:31
msgid "Leave it off for plugins you do not check often. Turn it on only for plugins where a bad update would be costly, such as a shop or booking plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:34
msgid "Applies the block to all plugins, or only to the plugins you pick in the list below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:35
msgid "Picking specific plugins lets everything else keep updating itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:38
msgid "The plugins in this list are never updated automatically. All other plugins update as usual."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:39
msgid "Use it for sensitive plugins (shop, booking, page builder) that you update by hand after a backup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:40
msgid "A plugin on this list stays outdated until you update it by hand, security fixes included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:43
msgid "Themes are no longer updated automatically. You can still update them by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:44
msgid "The design of the site never changes overnight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/DisableAutoUpdates/help.php:45
