#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:31
msgid "A mistyped address leads visitors to an error page, so open the button once after saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:34
msgid "Opens the button address in a new browser tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:35
msgid "The visitor keeps your page open in the old tab and can come back to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:36
msgid "Turn it off for a link inside your own site, or when the button only closes the popup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:39
msgid "Background color of the popup window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:40
msgid "Pick a color that stands out from your page but keeps the text readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:43
msgid "Color of the headline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:44
msgid "Needs enough contrast with the background color, otherwise the headline is hard to read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:47
msgid "Color of the text under the headline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:48
msgid "Needs enough contrast with the background color for visitors with weaker eyesight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:51
msgid "Background color of the button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:52
msgid "The button should be the most visible spot of the popup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:55
msgid "Color of the text on the button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:56
msgid "Keep it in strong contrast with the button background."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:59
msgid "How strongly the page behind the popup is darkened, from 0 (not at all) to 100 (black)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:60
msgid "A darker overlay pulls the attention to the popup, a light one keeps the page visible behind it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:63
msgid "For this many seconds after the page loads the popup cannot appear, whatever the visitor does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:64
msgid "Stops the popup from jumping at someone who has just arrived and moves the mouse out of the window by accident."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:65
msgid "With 0 the popup can appear at once, which feels pushy and may hurt your search ranking on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:68
msgid "How often the same visitor sees the popup: once per browser session, once every set number of days, or on every page view."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:69
msgid "Once per session or per several days is polite. A returning visitor is not asked the same thing again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:70
msgid "\"Every page view\" shows the popup again and again and annoys visitors. The days option remembers the visitor with a cookie, so it needs your cookie notice to mention it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:73
msgid "Shows the popup when the mouse leaves the browser window upwards, which usually means the visitor is going for the tab bar or the close button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:74
msgid "The classic exit intent. It works only with a mouse, so it does nothing on phones and tablets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:75
msgid "Turn it off when you rely on another trigger only, for example inactivity or time on page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:78
msgid "How many milliseconds the mouse must stay outside the window before the popup opens (1000 ms is one second)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:79
msgid "A short delay lets the popup ignore a quick slip of the mouse that returns at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:82
msgid "Shows the popup when the visitor switches to another browser tab or minimizes the window. The popup is waiting when they come back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:83
msgid "It also works on phones, where there is no mouse to leave the window with."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:84
msgid "Many people switch tabs only to check a message, so the popup can appear to someone who had no intention to leave."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:87
msgid "Shows the popup when the browser window loses focus, for example after a click into another program."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:88
msgid "Catches visitors who leave for another application without leaving the mouse path of the window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:89
msgid "A click into a video, a map or another embedded part of the page can count as losing focus and open the popup by mistake. Test the pages that have such parts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:90
msgid "Leave it off if you already use the tab switch trigger, the two overlap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:93
msgid "Shows the popup when the visitor does nothing (no mouse, keyboard, touch or scrolling) for a set time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:94
msgid "Reaches people who stopped reading and may be about to leave."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:95
msgid "A visitor who reads a long article without touching anything gets the popup in the middle of the text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:98
msgid "How many seconds of inactivity must pass before the popup opens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:99
msgid "A longer time is safer for pages with long texts. 30 seconds suits short pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:102
msgid "Shows the popup when the visitor quickly scrolls back up the page, which is a typical gesture before leaving on a phone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:103
msgid "A replacement of the mouse exit trigger for touch screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:104
msgid "Someone who scrolls up to re-read a paragraph may get the popup by mistake. Raise the pixel limit if it appears too often."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:107
msgid "How many pixels the page must jump up within a moment to count as a fast scroll up on a computer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:108
msgid "A higher number means only a big jump counts, so the popup appears less often."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:111
msgid "The same limit for phones and tablets, in pixels."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:112
msgid "Screens are shorter, so the default is lower than for a computer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:115
msgid "Shows the popup after this many seconds on the page, without waiting for any exit gesture. 0 turns this trigger off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:116
msgid "Works on every device and does not depend on what the visitor does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/ExitPopup/help.php:117
msgid "It is not an exit popup any more, it interrupts a visitor who may be reading. Use a long time, and mind that very early popups on mobile can hurt search ranking."
