#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:16
msgid "Login, registration, lost password and comments ask for a quick check before they are accepted. With the key-less Shield the browser of the visitor solves a small puzzle by itself: a fraction of a second, no account, no keys, no cookies, nothing sent to a third party. A visitor without JavaScript answers a simple sum instead, so nobody is locked out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:17
msgid "The Shield stops mass scripted attempts. It does not tell a person from a clever script: an attacker who spends the computing time passes, only slower. A visitor whose browser blocks the script sees the sum after a few seconds. Five wrong answers count as failed logins and lock the address like wrong passwords do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:18
msgid "When you use Cloudflare Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys or a CAPTCHA plugin instead, or when you want to protect only the forms of the Forms module."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:19
msgid "A CAPTCHA is already set up (turned on, keys stored or a CAPTCHA plugin active), or the site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare: the Shield limits per IP address, and behind such a proxy every visitor looks the same."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:22
msgid "Automatic uses keys from the central app while the site is connected, then your own Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys, and the key-less Shield when there are none. Anything you choose by hand is used as it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:23
msgid "Choosing the Shield on a site that has Turnstile or reCAPTCHA keys drops that check: the Shield is lighter and has no network of other sites behind it. Choosing a provider without its keys switches the CAPTCHA off silently."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:24
msgid "Leave it on Automatic unless you need one specific provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:25
msgid "Same as the CAPTCHA switch: a CAPTCHA is already set up, a CAPTCHA plugin is active or the site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:28
msgid "Switches comments off on the whole site: the comment forms, the Comments menu and the comment feeds disappear. Existing comments stay in the database but are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:29
msgid "A site that lives from discussion or from product reviews loses them. With WooCommerce the pack switches comments off on posts and pages only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:30
msgid "When visitors should be able to comment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:31
msgid "A plugin that disables comments is already active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:34
msgid "After the set number of wrong passwords (3 by default) the visitor's IP address is locked out for the lockout time (30 minutes by default, longer after repeated lockouts)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:35
msgid "Behind a proxy every visitor looks like the same IP address, so a few typos could lock everybody out. People who share one office address share the limit too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:36
msgid "When the site is behind a proxy that hides the real IP address and you did not set the IP source in Security > Firewall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:37
msgid "The site is behind a reverse proxy that is not Cloudflare, or a login protection plugin is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:40
msgid "Nobody can register or rename a user to a reserved name such as admin, administrator, root or test (any name that contains one of them as a word, for example \"my-admin\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:41
msgid "Accounts that already exist are not touched; a new account just cannot take such a name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:42
msgid "When you really need an account with a reserved name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:43
msgid "The login attempt limit is not set (this option works together with it)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:46
msgid "A failed login with a reserved name such as admin locks the IP address at once for the lockout time, without waiting for the maximum number of attempts. Bots try \"admin\" first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:47
msgid "It also applies to a real account with such a name: one typo in its password locks that IP address, maybe your own. Behind a shared proxy address it could lock everybody out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:48
msgid "When an account with a reserved name has to stay, or when you often mistype."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:49
msgid "An existing account uses a reserved name (rename it first), or the login attempt limit is not set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:52
msgid "The login page no longer tells whether the username or the password was wrong. Application Passwords are turned off, so new ones cannot be created. Messages about a lockout, CAPTCHA and two-step verification stay readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:53
msgid "Integrations that sign in with an Application Password stop working: the WordPress mobile app, REST clients, some MCP servers and publishing tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:54
msgid "When you use such an integration, or want to create Application Passwords again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:55
msgid "Somebody already has an Application Password (the pack never cuts off existing ones)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:58
msgid "Feed addresses (posts, comments, categories, search) answer 403 and the feed links leave the page head."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:59
msgid "RSS readers, newsletter tools with RSS campaigns, podcast apps and aggregators stop getting your updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:60
msgid "When anybody follows the site by RSS or e-mail from the feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:61
msgid "The site has more than 5 published posts, a feed plugin is active (Mailchimp for WP, podcast or aggregator plugins), or a plugin that disables feeds is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:64
msgid "The server refuses to hand out wp-config.php and its copies (.bak, .old, .zip, ...), which hold the database password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:65
msgid "It is a rule in .htaccess, which only Apache and LiteSpeed read. A wrong rule can break the whole site with an HTTP 500, so the pack checks the site afterwards and takes the rules back if it fails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:66
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:78
msgid "When the server configuration already blocks these files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:67
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:73
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:79
msgid "The server is not Apache or LiteSpeed (nginx, IIS), or the .htaccess file cannot be written."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:70
msgid "A folder without an index file, for example /wp-content/uploads/, answers 403 instead of showing the list of its files (Options -Indexes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:71
msgid "On some hosts the setting of .htaccess does not allow the Options line and the site answers HTTP 500. The pack detects it, takes only this line back and keeps the other rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:72
msgid "When you offer a file list on purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:76
msgid "readme.html, license.txt and wp-config-sample.php answer 403, so nobody can read the WordPress version from them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:77
msgid "Hardly any. A scanner that reads readme.html to find the version will not see it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:82
msgid "?author=1 no longer redirects to an author page that shows the login name, and the public list of users in the REST API is closed to visitors. Logged-in users keep it. The WordPress users sitemap (wp-sitemap-users.xml) is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:83
msgid "A decoupled front end (headless) or an app that reads authors over the REST API without logging in stops getting them. The block editor and the admin work as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:84
msgid "When a separate front end or an app needs the public list of users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:85
msgid "A decoupled front end plugin is active (WPGraphQL, Faust.js, WPGatsby), or a plugin that blocks user enumeration is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:88
msgid "The user name in the address of an author page (and in the REST \"slug\") is replaced with a code, for example /author/3f9a.../. The old /author/name/ addresses answer 404, there is no redirect. The sitemap and the theme links use the new addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:89
msgid "Author pages that are already indexed or linked stop working, and an author sitemap of an SEO plugin changes its addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:90
msgid "When you want to keep the old author addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:91
msgid "The site has more than 5 published posts (its author pages may already be indexed)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:94
msgid "The old remote interface xmlrpc.php is closed. Attackers use it to guess passwords in bulk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:95
msgid "Old mobile apps, some publishing tools and the Jetpack connection through XML-RPC stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:96
msgid "When a tool you use still talks to xmlrpc.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:97
msgid "A plugin that disables XML-RPC is already active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:100
msgid "The WordPress version leaves the page head and the addresses of scripts and styles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:101
msgid "None noticeable. It only makes automatic scanners work a little harder; it does not replace updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:102
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:156
msgid "Hardly ever needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:103
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:109
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:145
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:157
#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:163
msgid "It is never left out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:106
msgid "The code editors for themes and plugins in wp-admin are turned off (DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT). A stolen administrator login then cannot easily turn into running code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:107
msgid "You change theme and plugin files over FTP, the file manager or your editor instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:108
msgid "When you edit code in the WordPress admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:112
msgid "Sends X-Frame-Options (other sites cannot show yours in a frame), X-Content-Type-Options and Referrer-Policy. The headers are set in .htaccess and also by PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:113
msgid "A page that has to be shown inside a frame of another site stops appearing there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:114
msgid "When other sites embed your pages on purpose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:115
msgid "It is never left out; where .htaccess cannot be written the headers are sent by PHP only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:118
msgid "The Permissions-Policy header turns off camera, microphone, location, payment and USB for the page and for frames inside it. It is sent by PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:119
msgid "Apple Pay and Google Pay, \"use my location\" on a map and video calls from the page stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:120
msgid "When the site needs any of these functions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:121
msgid "WooCommerce is active (online payments), or a plugin that sets the same header is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:124
msgid "Every request to http:// is redirected to https:// (a rule in .htaccess)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:125
msgid "Behind Cloudflare in the Flexible mode or another proxy that talks to the server over http this causes an endless redirect and the site does not open. The pack checks it and takes the rule back. Insecure content (http images) on a page is blocked by browsers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:126
msgid "When the site does not work over https everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:127
msgid "The site address is not https, this page was not opened over https, plain http does not answer, or the site is behind a proxy that is not Cloudflare."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:130
msgid "Tells the browser to open the site only over https for a whole year, even when somebody types http://."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:131
msgid "The browser remembers it for a year and cannot be talked out of it. If the certificate expires or https breaks, visitors cannot open the site at all until it works again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:132
msgid "Before the site works over https everywhere, including the subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:133
msgid "The starter pack never switches it on. Switch it on yourself when you are sure about https."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:136
msgid "Every request is redirected to one version of the address (with or without www, http or https) taken from the site address in Settings > General (a rule in .htaccess)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:137
msgid "A wrong site address in Settings > General, or a proxy that talks to the server over http, causes an endless redirect and the site does not open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:138
msgid "When the redirect to one address is already done by the server or a CDN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:139
msgid "The starter pack never switches it on. Switch it on yourself when you are sure about the site address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:142
msgid "WordPress keeps only the last 10 saved versions of each post and page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:143
msgid "You cannot go back to a version older than the tenth one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:144
msgid "When you need a long history of changes of your texts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:148
msgid "The background messages between the editor and the server (autosave, post locking) go once a minute instead of every 15 to 60 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:149
msgid "When two people edit one post, they see each other's changes and the post lock a little later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:150
msgid "When many editors work on the same texts at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:151
msgid "A caching plugin that already manages Heartbeat is active (WP Rocket, LiteSpeed Cache, Perfmatters, Heartbeat Control)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:154
msgid "Removes the emoji script and style that WordPress adds to every page. Emoji still show, with the font of the visitor's device."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:155
msgid "A very old browser without an emoji font shows empty boxes instead of emoji."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:160
msgid "Deletes the Twenty* themes that WordPress brought itself and that nothing uses; the newest one stays as the fallback. A theme you installed yourself is never deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:161
msgid "A deleted theme has to be installed again when you want it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:162
msgid "When you want to keep the default themes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:166
msgid "Every request from a banned address, range or country is refused with a 403 page, whatever it asks for: pages, login, admin or REST API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:167
msgid "Blocked visitors see only the block page. Administrators who are logged in and addresses on the allowlist are never blocked, so you cannot lock yourself out while you are signed in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:168
msgid "A wrong ban or a wrong \"Client IP source\" can block real visitors, or your own address once you log out. Add your own address to the allowlist first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:169
msgid "Leave it off when the server or Cloudflare already filters addresses for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:172
msgid "Tells the firewall where to read the visitor's address from. \"Direct connection\" uses the address the server sees on the connection (REMOTE_ADDR). Behind Cloudflare or another reverse proxy that address is the proxy, so the real visitor is read from a header the proxy adds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:173
msgid "The right choice makes bans and lockouts hit the real visitor. Headers are trusted only when the request really comes from Cloudflare (or from a proxy range of your own), because anybody can fake a header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:174
msgid "Direct connection behind a proxy makes all visitors look like one address: one ban or lockout then blocks everybody. Choosing Cloudflare or a reverse proxy on a site that is not behind one lets a visitor pretend to be another address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:175
msgid "Leave \"Direct connection\" unless you are sure the site sits behind Cloudflare or a reverse proxy (the host can tell you)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:178
msgid "Addresses that are never blocked, one per line. You can write a single address (203.0.113.7) or a whole range in [[cidr|CIDR]] notation (203.0.113.0/24). The loopback address 127.0.0.1, the computer talking to itself, is always allowed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:179
msgid "These visitors pass the firewall and the country blocklist even when a ban would match them. Put your office, your monitoring and your payment gateway here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:180
msgid "Everybody behind an address on this list is trusted, so list only addresses you control. A shared or changing address (home internet) is a poor choice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:183
msgid "The sentence a blocked visitor sees on the 403 page. Empty shows a plain default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:184
msgid "Say how to reach you, so a visitor who is blocked by mistake can ask for help."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:187
msgid "Visitors whose address belongs to one of the countries below are refused by the IP firewall. The address ranges of each country are downloaded and stored on the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:188
msgid "Traffic from those countries, including real customers, search engine robots and monitoring tools, sees only the block page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:189
msgid "Country data is never exact: a visitor on a VPN or a traveler can be blocked or let through by mistake. Blocking a country also blocks every bot or service whose servers stand there, for example search engines."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:190
msgid "Use it only against a clear, repeated attack from specific countries. It is not a general protection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:193
msgid "The countries to block. The list is applied when you save the settings: the address ranges of each chosen country are downloaded and a ban is created or refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:194
msgid "Every visitor from these countries is blocked as soon as the country blocklist is on. Removing a country lifts the block for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:195
msgid "Do not block the country where your customers, your host or your payment gateway are. Blocking your own country can lock you out once you log out; add your address to the allowlist first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:198
msgid "The login page moves from wp-login.php to the address you choose below. Anybody who opens the old address gets the response chosen under \"Direct wp-login.php behavior\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:199
msgid "Bots that hammer wp-login.php find nothing. People who log in must use the new address, so give it to everybody who logs in and bookmark it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:200
msgid "If you forget the new address you cannot log in. Rescue: add define( 'UXSTUDIO_DISABLE_LOGIN_LOCK', true ); to wp-config.php. Plugins and saved links that point to wp-login.php stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:201
msgid "Leave it off if several people log in and you cannot make sure they know the new address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:204
msgid "The new address of the login page, for example \"my-login\" gives yourdomain.com/my-login."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:205
msgid "Pick something that is not easy to guess. If it clashes with an existing page, the change is not applied and a warning is logged, so the old login keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:206
msgid "Write the address down before you save. Without it you cannot reach the login page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:209
msgid "What a visitor gets who opens wp-login.php or wp-admin without being logged in, once the custom login address is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:210
msgid "A 404 page looks as if there is no login at all. A redirect or a message tells honest visitors where they are, but also shows the page exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:211
msgid "Choosing the homepage or another page for a visitor who really wants to log in can confuse them. Make sure your team knows the new login address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:214
msgid "The page of your site that a visitor of the old login address is sent to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:215
msgid "Pick a harmless public page, for example the homepage or a contact page. Used only with \"Existing page\" above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:216
msgid "A page that is deleted or turned into a draft later leaves visitors on an error page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:219
msgid "How many wrong passwords from one address are tolerated before that address is locked out. The default is 3."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:220
msgid "A lower number stops password guessing sooner but also catches people who simply mistype. Three to five is a sensible range."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:221
msgid "A very low number (1 or 2) can lock out you or your client after a typo. People who share one address, such as an office, share the count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:224
msgid "For how many minutes a locked-out address cannot try to log in. The default is 30. With \"Lengthen repeated lockouts\" the time grows with every repeat."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:225
msgid "A longer lockout slows down attackers more, but a person who locked themselves out has to wait that long."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:226
msgid "A very long lockout on a shared address keeps everybody behind it out for hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:229
msgid "Sends an e-mail each time an address gets locked out. It names the address, the username that was tried and the length of the lockout. The e-mail goes to the address set below, or to the site administrator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:230
msgid "You learn about attacks at once. On a site that is attacked all day it can mean dozens of e-mails, so it fits a quiet site best."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:231
msgid "Leave it off if the site is a regular target of bots and you do not want your inbox full."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:234
msgid "When an address has had several failed logins recently (the threshold set under \"Adaptive mode threshold\"), it gets the next harder Shield difficulty for 15 minutes. The Shield is the key-less [[CAPTCHA]] of UX Studio: the browser solves a small puzzle by itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:235
msgid "A normal visitor still gets the easy check. Only addresses that look like an attack must compute longer, so the cost lands on the attacker."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:238
msgid "Decides when the check is required in the inline form. \"Always\" asks every visitor. \"Adaptive\" asks only after repeated failed attempts from that address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:239
msgid "Adaptive is friendlier: most visitors see no check at all. Always protects better against the very first attempt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:240
msgid "With Adaptive an attacker gets a few free attempts before the check appears. Always puts a small extra step in front of every honest visitor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:243
msgid "In adaptive mode, how many failed attempts from one address make the [[CAPTCHA]] appear. Allowed values are 1 to 20."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:244
msgid "A low number starts the check early; a high number lets an attacker try more before it shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:247
msgid "Turns off the extra embed machinery of WordPress: other sites can no longer discover your embed address, pasted links to sites that are not on the WordPress list of known services are no longer turned into embeds, and the embed preview in the visual editor goes away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:248
msgid "The page head is a little lighter. Links to well-known services such as YouTube still become players as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:249
msgid "Other WordPress sites can no longer show your posts as embedded cards. Pasted links to less common sites stay plain links instead of becoming a box. Check posts that rely on such embeds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:250
msgid "Leave it off if you want others to embed your posts, or you paste links to uncommon sites and expect a box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:253
msgid "Anonymous visitors are refused by the [[REST API]], the technical interface that apps, forms and many plugins use. Logged-in users keep full access. A list of well-known public endpoints (forms, shop, oEmbed) stays open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:254
msgid "Bots can no longer read your content and user names through the interface. Pages themselves look the same."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:255
msgid "A plugin, mobile app, newsletter tool, headless front end or contact form that calls the REST API without logging in can stop working. Test the forms and the shop after you turn it on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:256
msgid "Leave it off when other services read your site through the REST API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:259
msgid "Only common file types can be uploaded: images, PDF and Office documents, ZIP, MP3, MP4, WebM and web fonts. Everything else is refused in the media library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:260
msgid "Nobody can upload a risky or unusual file type by mistake or by a stolen account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:261
msgid "Other file types, for example 3D models, CAD drawings, special audio or code files, can no longer be uploaded. Users will get an error and not know why."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:262
msgid "Leave it off when your team regularly uploads types that are not in the list above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:265
msgid "Hides Posts from the admin menu and the admin bar, sends the Posts screens in the admin back to the dashboard and removes the Quick Draft box. On the site every blog post, category, tag, date and author page is sent to the homepage with a permanent (301) redirect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:266
msgid "A presentation site without a blog looks tidier in the admin. A visitor who opens an old post address lands on the homepage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:267
msgid "Existing posts disappear for visitors and search engines, which can cost you search traffic, and browsers remember a permanent redirect for a long time. You also cannot edit posts in the admin any more. Plugins that store their content as posts (news, events) are affected too. The posts stay in the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/SecurityOptimization/help.php:268
msgid "Leave it off if the site has a blog or a plugin stores its content as posts."
msgstr ""

