#: includes/Modules/VulnerabilityScanner/help.php:12
msgid "The scanner sends the list of your plugins, themes and their versions to the central app. The central app compares it with a database of known security holes (Wordfence Intelligence) and sends back what it found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/VulnerabilityScanner/help.php:13
msgid "You see confirmed vulnerabilities for the exact versions installed here, not just \"a newer version exists\". Only names and versions leave the site, no content and no visitor data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Modules/VulnerabilityScanner/help.php:14
msgid "Without it the scanner only knows that a newer version exists on WordPress.org. It cannot tell whether your version has a known hole, so an empty result is not an all-clear. The check also needs the site to be paired with the central app via Content Sync."
